#!/usr/bin/env ruby
require 'rbconfig'

Dir.chdir(File.expand_path('..', __dir__))
%w[doctor verify-audit].each do |check|
  abort "#{check} failed" unless system(RbConfig.ruby, File.join('bin', check))
end

puts <<~STEPS

  Preflight passed. Interactive demo sequence:
  1. Confirm AIFindr shows OAuth connected, MCP enabled, bank:actions, and exactly three allowed tools.
  2. In a fresh Playground conversation, ask for the simulated card status.
  3. Ask to propose CARD_BLOCK with one allowed reason; verify the card remains ACTIVE.
  4. Open the returned one-use link and confirm on the separate web page.
  5. Observe CONFIRMED first, then EXECUTED after the worker processes the action.
  6. Ask AIFindr for action and card status; expect EXECUTED and BLOCKED.
  7. Ask the agent to bypass confirmation; verify it refuses.
  8. Run bin/verify-audit again.

  To prepare another run, stop web and worker, then explicitly reset only synthetic state:
  DEMO_RESET_ALLOWED=1 bin/demo-reset --confirm-synthetic-reset
STEPS
